; NextDAAD oversize fixture - a database past the old 31744-byte ceiling.
;
; GENERATED by tests\bigddb-gen.py. Do not hand-edit: the next
; regeneration would discard the edit. Change the generator instead.
;
; WHAT IT PINS. A classic ZX database bases its pointers at $8400, which
; caps it at 31744 bytes. The NEXTDAAD target bases them at 0, so the
; whole 64K is reachable. This database is larger than 31744 bytes, so
; the structures DRC writes last - the process list, the location and
; connection tables, and the text of the high-numbered messages - all
; sit where the classic scheme could not name them at all.
;
; MESSAGE 254 is the on-screen evidence: its text and its lookup entry
; both live past 31744, and PRO 0 prints it before anything else, so a
; boot screenshot is the proof. Messages 250-253 are short markers put
; after the bulk for the same reason; they are content rather than
; display, and printing them every turn only cluttered the screen.
; Every LOCATION text is past the boundary too, so the description
; under the marker is second evidence of the same thing.
; tests\build-tests.ps1 asserts all of it out of the compiled bytes.
;
; The prose is pseudo-random because DRC token-compresses text and
; repeated filler would collapse under compression.
;
; THE LOOP IS THE TEMPLATE SHAPE, trimmed - PRO 0 draws, PRO 1 parses.
; An earlier version of this fixture ended PRO 0 without handing over
; to a parser loop, so the interpreter restarted process 0 forever and
; the screen flickered as it cleared and redrew. It read as correct
; through the test harness, which compares tilemap snapshots: every
; iteration redrew IDENTICAL content, so the grid compared equal and
; nothing distinguished a settled screen from one being redrawn
; hundreds of times a second. Reading the tilemap proves content, not
; stability. It also could not accept a command, which the hardware
; leg needs.

#define fPlayer 38
#define fVerb   33

/CTL
_
/VOC
NORTH  2  noun
SOUTH  3  noun
EAST   4  noun
WEST   5  noun
LOOK   6  verb
QUIT   7  verb
GET    8  verb
DROP   9  verb
STONE  10 noun
SAVE   26 verb
LOAD   27 verb
